Atrous is a modified fork of herdr-app / herdr-core by herdrdev
(https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app, https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-core),
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE). This repository is the
app (herdr-app); the core lives at https://github.com/zecod/atrous-core.

Changes from herdr-app 0.1.13, made by the Atrous authors:
- Rebranded: the app, its CLI and Cargo package are `atrous`; the window and
  bundle id is io.github.zecod.atrous; its home is ~/.config/atrous
  (ATROUS_HOME); every HERDR_* environment variable is ATROUS_*, and the core
  it uses is atrous-core / `atc` (ATC_* variables), so it runs side by side
  with herdr-app without sharing anything.
- The herdr logo (the ram) and sheep artwork are removed and replaced by the
  Atrous mark, including the macOS disk image background; the Herdr 98
  layout and its art are removed. Apache-2.0 grants no trademark rights; Atrous
  uses no herdr marks as its own.
- First-start migration of the person's own files from ~/.config/herdr-app
  (read only) into ~/.config/atrous.
- The mod module is "atrous", with "herdr" kept as an alias; core() is the new
  name for hc().
- Fedra (fedra/) is the built-in UI and default layout; Settings, the
  first-run flow and the stock panels are Atrous's own.
- Usage telemetry removed; feedback opens a GitHub issue instead of posting to
  herdr's service; updates come from GitHub releases of zecod/atrous and
  zecod/atrous-core. No requests go to herdr's servers.
- Installers, packaging, release workflow and documentation adapted to the
  new names and endpoints.

Files changed for the fork carry no per-file notice beyond this one. Original
copyright and attribution notices from herdr-app are kept, and third-party
notices are in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES. Patches in vendor/ marked HERDR: are
herdr-app's; patches marked ATROUS: are Atrous's.
